  "result": "Based on the search results, the document that records this decision is **ADR-018** (Architecture Decision Record 018), which explicitly covers the decision to queue webhook deliveries instead of calling customer HTTP endpoints inline.\n\nThe document details:\n- **The original alternative**: ADR-005 originally imagined sending HTTP calls inline from the event handler in the same request\n- **Why it was rejected**: A slow or unreachable webhook endpoint would stall the original request that triggered the event, creating unnecessary latency coupling\n- **The chosen approach**: Queue deliveries with exponential backoff retry logic (capped at a maximum attempt ceiling)\n- **Supporting requirements**: REQ-154 (deliveries queued, never inline), REQ-156 (exponential backoff), and REQ-157 (attempt ceiling)\n\nThe document includes the context of how this decision emerged, the specific latency problem identified by Kaya Ferreira during implementation in March 2026, and the retry semantics requirements that couldn't fit into a single inline attempt.\n\nANSWER: docs/adr/ADR-018-webhook-retry-policy.md",
